<article class="env-lemma" id="54BBAE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/54BBAE">Lemma <span data-tag="54BBAE">5.3.2.7</span>.</a> Let $f: \calA \rightarrow \calB $ be a right exact functor between $\infty $-categories, and let $A \in \calA $ be an initial object. Then $f(A)$ is an initial object of $\calB $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $B$ be an object of $\calB $. Proposition <a href="/tag/16A55E" data-tag="16A55E">5.3.2.5</a> implies that $\calA ' = \calB _{/B} \times _{\calB } \calA $ is filtered. We may identify $\bHom _{\calB }(f(A), B)$ with the fiber of the right fibration $\calA ' \rightarrow \calA $ over the object $A$. We now apply Lemma <a href="/tag/A23547" data-tag="A23547">5.3.2.6</a> to deduce that $\bHom _{\calB }(f(A),B)$ is contractible. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>